{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464935-health-levels-alternatives","id":1464935,"title":"Health Levels... Alternatives","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-22T16:27:24-07:00","id":1464935,"title":"Health Levels... Alternatives","content":"There are forcefields, bio-mods and armor. What other ways are there to add &quot;ticks&quot; onto the worrisome 7 health levels?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T19:29:17-07:00","id":1464955,"title":"","content":"Life can always add more (not sure if at 3 or 4 - 5 can make 'em skyrocket, as that would be needed for the most outrageous self-transmutations like becoming a dragon), I think Prime can be used to &quot;reinforce your pattern&quot; for the same effect at high levels. Prob a combination of these are used in the bio-mods and some of the Cybernetic implants that do just that (I think the one that reinforces the bone structure gives 2 extra hp)<br /> <br /> Armor, ironically, doesn't (unless I'm missing something): It adds Soak to keep 'em safe, wich it's different - albeit if by &quot;armor&quot; you mean a giant &quot;mecha&quot;, that could probably be better represented trough the rules about objects (like with cars or tanks), which would provide a layer of &quot;hp&quot; over your hp against some kinds of assaults.<br /> <br /> If you're interested in protection, well the best way it's not being there (and there are a lot of magical means to that end). But that's a bit of a moot answer, isn't it? - still, making the attacks fail trough increasing the difficulty of the attacker it's a compromise, and one that can also be achieved trough a lot of means (including low-key forcefields). Entropy it's the queen here.<br /> <br /> The Rote &quot;Gift of Prana&quot; (Life 3/Prime 2) provides an interesting alternative in a &quot;pool of hp&quot; that's used as a reservoir of regeneration that activates on harm (doesn't give you more &quot;ticks&quot;, but renews the ticks you lose)<br /> <br /> Then you have those that decide to ignore the process altogether by negating the result of loosing them all: Like with the self-resurrection machine in the basic (a techno-magical Talisman with a TON of Spheres on it that allows you to pretty much &quot;save&quot; a copy of yourself to activate at the moment of your death) - you can prob. have &quot;cheaper&quot; alternatives to not die when you die, like shifting to an astral body triggered on the moment before death with Mind 5/Time 4/Entropy 1, and things like that.<br /> Some mages-turned-undead-abomination can keep alive with no HP as long as they didn't &quot;die&quot; of aggravated damage. Prob. there are more than one way to similarly negate (or delay) the &quot;you die&quot; effect on loosing your hp","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T22:24:18-07:00","id":1465096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464935-health-levels-alternatives?p=1464955#post1464955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Rote &quot;Gift of Prana&quot; (Life 3/Prime 2) provides an interesting alternative in a &quot;pool of hp&quot; that's used as a reservoir of regeneration that activates on harm (doesn't give you more &quot;ticks&quot;, but renews the ticks you lose)</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you cast it on someone else (as Gift would seem to imply)?<br /> Does it cost Quintessence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T02:06:07-07:00","id":1465109,"title":"","content":"Time 3 can be used to rewind a few moments, negating a successful attack. Pretty awesome when used to save a person in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T07:55:07-07:00","id":1465137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464935-health-levels-alternatives?p=1465109#post1465109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time 3 can be used to rewind a few moments, negating a successful attack. Pretty awesome when used to save a person in combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is awesome, but it generates more paradox than other vulgar effects. The RAW for reversing time are brutal (but still worth it in many circumstances).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T09:04:18-07:00","id":1465146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>breggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464935-health-levels-alternatives?p=1465137#post1465137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is awesome, but it generates more paradox than other vulgar effects. The RAW for reversing time are brutal (but still worth it in many circumstances).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it is better to get some Paradox than to suffer a mortal wound or be defeated in an important engagement. The Paradox is a problem for later, and can be dealt with in multiple ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T05:36:02-07:00","id":1465269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464935-health-levels-alternatives?p=1465096#post1465096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you cast it on someone else (as Gift would seem to imply)?<br /> Does it cost Quintessence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. If you want to cast on yourself Life 2 it's enough. (And it's Prime 3, not 2 - it's an enchantment on a living being). The system it's: Spend success on duration and targeting (it was a Revised rote) and spend a point of Quintessence to enchant the target. After that each succcess creates a healing pool of 2 hp. If the target it's injured before the end of the duration this pool heals the injury as much as possible. This rote can be Vulgar or not depending on the kind of wounds that would be able to heal - defined at the moment of casting (Bashing Damage it's coincidental, Lethal it's usualy Vulgar unless it's only for minor wounds, Aggravated it's always Vulgar). Also, if the effect it's Vulgar the caster has to decide if it's going to work in pressence of Witnesses. If yes, then it's Vulgar with Witnesses even if there wasn't anyone present at the moment of casting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T05:01:44-07:00","id":1465382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464935-health-levels-alternatives?p=1465146#post1465146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it is better to get some Paradox than to suffer a mortal wound or be defeated in an important engagement. The Paradox is a problem for later, and can be dealt with in multiple ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, and I said as much in my post... &quot;... still worth it in many circumstances.&quot; My current character, an IterationX (technically cyborg, but he hates that term and always corrects people) has Time 3. I rarely use it, but when I do it's really impressive.<br /> <br /> To add more to the conversation, I can share the methods my character uses to be physically tough.<br /> <br /> First, he has Skeletal Enhancement and 1 level of armor from the Enhancements background. This gives him +2 health levels and +1 soak die (ST ruled that because it's internal armor it applies to everything, not just physical attacks, and it's only one level).<br /> <br /> Second, he keeps a complex procedure active that gives +1 autosoak and converts lethal to bashing (Forces 2). It also allows him to soak aggravated damage (Prime 3) with stamina. He has Stamina 4.<br /> <br /> So that gives me 9 health levels and a base of 5 soak dice against all forms of damage, with +1 automatic success added. 10's count double because of Stamina 4 (we use the double-rule rather than the &quot;10's explode&quot; rule, it's faster in play). He also wears light body armor at almost all times (+2 soak dice), and he is about to learn Matter 3 which will allow him to create even better body armor.<br /> <br /> He also has Life 2/Matter 2 to heal himself (ST ruled he also needs matter to heal himself because of his extensive cybernetics), and also Prime 3 so he can set up an automatic healing in advance as per some of the above conversation.<br /> <br /> There are many many ways that almost any mage can make themselves really tough to kill. Of course, he's no shock trooper - most of his toughness is meant as mere story. He thinks of himself as a field-scientist, and avoids combat where possible, as would most mages regardless of their Convention/Tradition.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26904,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","user":"breggie","date":". 10-26-2021, 08:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T05:32:27-07:00","id":1465386,"title":"","content":"I think just about every Sphere has some defensive application against physical injury. <br /> <br /> Correspondence can be used to make your sim more accurate; it should also be able to mess with someone else's aim, making you harder to hit. <br /> <br /> Entropy can cause misfires. <br /> <br /> Forces can erect force fields. <br /> <br /> Life can directly boost your toughness \u2014 as well as your ability to dodge, when that matters. <br /> <br /> Matter can strengthen your garments, letting them serve as armor \u2014 or <i>better</i> armor, if it's already armor. <br /> <br /> Mind can let you cloud men's minds; if they can't see you, it's harder to shoot you. <br /> <br /> Prime can imbue weapons to make them inflict aggravated damage; I would think that it ought to be able to reinforce armor to better withstand it. <br /> <br /> Spirit\u2026 I'd have to think about that one. <br /> <br /> Time, as stated, can be used for a Mulligan. <br /> <br /> Most of those don't give you health levels; instead, they make it less likely you'll get hit in the first place. Which might be better; if you can avoid being hit, you won't <i>need</i> health levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T07:10:05-07:00","id":1465509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464935-health-levels-alternatives?p=1465386#post1465386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forces can erect force fields.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Forces 2 can either deflect attacks (adding to the difficulty of the enemy's attack roll), or dampen the force of an attack (change lethal into bashing and add +1 automatic soak success).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464935-health-levels-alternatives?p=1465386#post1465386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Life can directly boost your toughness \u2014 as well as your ability to dodge, when that matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Life 3 or 4 can add health levels (I think, not 100% on this), and it can also allow you to soak aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464935-health-levels-alternatives?p=1465386#post1465386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prime can imbue weapons to make them inflict aggravated damage; I would think that it ought to be able to reinforce armor to better withstand it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prime2/Matter2 can make weapons/armor inflict/withstand aggravated damage. Prime3/Life2 can do the same for oneself, or Prime3/Life3 for someone else.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T16:03:48-07:00","id":1465710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464935-health-levels-alternatives?p=1465386#post1465386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirit\u2026 I'd have to think about that one.</div> </div> </div> </div>An Umbrood Symbiant who can substitute Essence for a human's health levels.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T06:01:58-07:00","id":1465757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>breggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464935-health-levels-alternatives?p=1465509#post1465509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Prime2/Matter2 can make weapons/armor inflict/withstand aggravated damage. Prime3/Life2 can do the same for oneself, or Prime3/Life3 for someone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two things:<br /> <br /> You shouldn't need to lock Prime effects. Locking only happens when you anchor a spell to a pattern of a type not contained in the spell, such as attaching a force field (a purely Forces effect) to a person (not Forces). A Prime 2 spell to enhance a pattern can easily be attached to the pattern it is already targeting without adding any additional spheres. Adding agg damage or resistance is only Prime 2.<br /> <br /> Also, locking spells is not any kind of alteration to the pattern so the difficulty doesn't go up when you target someone other than yourself. This isn't spelled explicitly anywhere that I am aware of, but the example of attaching an invisibility spell to a person (any person) is Forces 2/Life 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T11:33:41-07:00","id":1465794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464935-health-levels-alternatives?p=1465757#post1465757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Two things:<br /> <br /> You shouldn't need to lock Prime effects. Locking only happens when you anchor a spell to a pattern of a type not contained in the spell, such as attaching a force field (a purely Forces effect) to a person (not Forces). A Prime 2 spell to enhance a pattern can easily be attached to the pattern it is already targeting without adding any additional spheres. Adding agg damage or resistance is only Prime 2.<br /> <br /> Also, locking spells is not any kind of alteration to the pattern so the difficulty doesn't go up when you target someone other than yourself. This isn't spelled explicitly anywhere that I am aware of, but the example of attaching an invisibility spell to a person (any person) is Forces 2/Life 2.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok, but that isn't RAW, at least not in M20. The Prime entry is very explicit on M20 page 520.<br /> <br /> Prime 2<br /> &quot;Weapons or attacks infused with Quintessence through Prime 2 Effects may... inflict aggravated damage, and substances infused the same way may protect against such harm... On a related note, she may also - with Life 2 for simple organisms, or Life 3 for complex ones - consecrate a living thing at this Rank, as if that life-form were an object described above.&quot;<br /> <br /> Prime 3<br /> &quot;With such powers, she could (with Life 3) enchant a living thing so that it could inflict or endure aggravated damage...&quot;<br /> <br /> Am I somehow reading this wrong? I take it to mean that with Prime2 alone, you can make a weapon inflict or withstand aggravated damage. With Life3 added, you could make yourself or another complex organism inflict aggravated damage. Both applications cost 1 quintessence per attack. With Prime3/Life3, you could make yourself or another complex organism inflict aggravated damage with every attack or soak aggravated damage for the duration, no quintessence required.<br /> <br /> This interpretation is also reinforced in How Do You DO That, page 46 &quot;Consecrating and Energizing Items&quot; and page 47 &quot;Energizing Organisms&quot; (though the latter seems to imply you need Prime 3 only - we all know that HDYDT is inconsistent.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T12:14:09-07:00","id":1465800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>breggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464935-health-levels-alternatives?p=1465794#post1465794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ok, but that isn't RAW, at least not in M20. The Prime entry is very explicit on M20 page 520.<br /> <br /> Prime 2<br /> &quot;Weapons or attacks infused with Quintessence through Prime 2 Effects may... inflict aggravated damage, and substances infused the same way may protect against such harm... On a related note, she may also - with Life 2 for simple organisms, or Life 3 for complex ones - consecrate a living thing at this Rank, as if that life-form were an object described above.&quot;<br /> <br /> Prime 3<br /> &quot;With such powers, she could (with Life 3) enchant a living thing so that it could inflict or endure aggravated damage...&quot;<br /> <br /> Am I somehow reading this wrong? I take it to mean that with Prime2 alone, you can make a weapon inflict or withstand aggravated damage. With Life3 added, you could make yourself or another complex organism inflict aggravated damage. Both applications cost 1 quintessence per attack. With Prime3/Life3, you could make yourself or another complex organism inflict aggravated damage with every attack or soak aggravated damage for the duration, no quintessence required.<br /> <br /> This interpretation is also reinforced in How Do You DO That, page 46 &quot;Consecrating and Energizing Items&quot; and page 47 &quot;Energizing Organisms&quot; (though the latter seems to imply you need Prime 3 only - we all know that HDYDT is inconsistent.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well I agree that it takes Prime 3 to enhance a life pattern. As for the rest...not wrong, it just doesn't match rules elsewhere in M20.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> M20 pg 511</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Certain Effects, of course, travel because of the nature of the things they do; rumors circulate, winds and fires move, a shape-shifted character can run around, a gate leads to some other location, and so forth.<br /> <br /> If, however, you want to cast a lingering, mobile Effect that has been integrated into a specific Pattern and which involves a Sphere that is not normally related to that sort of Pattern, then the Effect must be \u201clocked\u201d into the target\u2019s Pattern by a Sphere that does apply to that Pattern.</div> </div> </div> </div>The pattern of a sword moves with the sword. That's why you only need Prime 2 to enhance a sword. You don't need Matter 2 to 'lock' the spell onto the object because it is already locked to the object's pattern by Prime. The pattern of a human moves with the human. What is different?<br /> <br /> When the sphere rules are contradictory I use the following test: When you see a sphere combination, ask what each Sphere is doing there. If there's not a good answer, it doesn't belong. That's the test HDYDT fails regularly, by the way, which is why I never bother with that book.<br /> <br /> Going back to this Prime 3 Life 3 spell to give a creature aggravated damage, what is Life 3 doing? It's not enhancing the pattern because Prime 3 can do that on its own. It's not locking the spell because we don't need anything to lock a Prime spell to a pattern. It doesn't seem to be anything other than an arbitrarily high sphere tax. It doesn't belong.<br /> <br /> Edit: I'm open to the possibility that Life is more resistant to Prime manipulation than other pattern spheres, but I don't think its necessary and I'd like to see that spelled out. If anything its the other way. Enhancing a living being without enhancing its pattern leads to pattern bleed. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 10-29-2021, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T12:31:21-07:00","id":1465805,"title":"","content":"I have to agree that, although it does help with some doubts and, well, establishes jurisprudence, good or bad, HDYDT is actually a terrible book in terms of making sense of the Sphere system. It frequently errs on the side of making for excessively high Sphere requirements for no good reason, sometimes in direct contradiction to previously established rules, like when it insists in making Spirit into a requirement for every single effect if the Mage is a shaman.<br /> <br /> That book formalizes a view on the magic system that is contrary to how it was intended for most of the game's existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T13:42:47-07:00","id":1465822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464935-health-levels-alternatives?p=1465805#post1465805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to agree that, although it does help with some doubts and, well, establishes jurisprudence, good or bad, HDYDT is actually a terrible book in terms of making sense of the Sphere system. It frequently errs on the side of making for excessively high Sphere requirements for no good reason, sometimes in direct contradiction to previously established rules, like when it insists in making Spirit into a requirement for every single effect if the Mage is a shaman.<br /> <br /> That book formalizes a view on the magic system that is contrary to how it was intended for most of the game's existence.</div> </div> </div> </div> I have to agree with you on this. As much as I appreciate Satyros Brucato's refinement of paradigm, his take on the lore, etc., it doesn't seem like he's super interested in being constrained by what the spheres are supposed to be able to do at any given level. When I read through &quot;Rich Bastard's Guide&quot; last night, I all but gave up on the rotes section; I'm waiting for someone to start whatever *THE* thread will be for discussion of the book (which I assume will be after it's available to people who didn't pre-order,) but suffice it to say that there's no reckoning the sphere requirements for a number of those rotes with what is actually written in the sphere write-ups in the core book for <i>any </i>edition of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T07:47:50-07:00","id":1465895,"title":"","content":"As much as I like brucato and his vision for mage, I have to agree that he's not exactly a nuts and bolts man. That said, the spirit thing in how do you do that gets more negativity than it deserves:<br /> <br /> First, it's entirely optional. Second, the mandated Spirit is something that the Mage ought to have anyway. Third, the mandated Spirit doesn't actually impact anything in terms of the practical use of the system: conjunctional spheres have no effect on the mechanics other than the binary \u201cdo you have what you need to do this?\u201d \u2014 which, going back to the second point, is always \u201cyes\u201d where this option or any variations thereof are concerned. So its biggest crime is that it doesn't do anything useful \u2014 which isn't much of a crime, all things considered, since one of the things it might have done, but didn't, would have been to <i>replace</i> the other Sphere requirements, turning Spirit into an uber-Sphere. So my reaction to it tends to be more along the lines of \u201cmeh\u201d rather than \u201coh, the horror; the horror!\u201d<br /> <br /> But again, Brucato doesn't seem to be much of a nuts and bolts guy. In fact, in a recent interview that he participated in, he mentioned that back in the day, the Mage development team didn't actually do much in the way of playing the game. In that regard, MRev's Malcolm Sheppard would be a superior pic for writing the game crunch; and I kind of wish that he had been involved in the development of M20.<br /> <br /> On a bit of a tangent, because I really want to get this off my chest: I've noticed a trend in the X5 game development that we have seen thus far (Vampire, Werewolf, and Hunter); and that is a tendency to borrow heavily from their Chronicles of Darkness counterparts. H5 is borrowing so heavily from HtV that is essentially a completely different game than HtR1e: no Imbued with Messenger-granted powers; just cells of hunters hunting monsters. I mention this because once they get around to M5, I won't mind if they borrow liberally from MtAw's Arcana. Not on big ways such as replacing Entropy with Death and Fate, mind you; but in subtler ways like revising correspondence and time to work the way awakening's Space and Time work; or changing the way wonders are created to something more along the lines of Awakening's imbued items. And the big one as far as this thread thus far is concerned: drastically scaling back on the need for conjunctional spheres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T09:24:56-07:00","id":1465908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464935-health-levels-alternatives?p=1465895#post1465895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, the spirit thing in how do you do that gets more negativity than it deserves\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is context. It would be perfectly fine in a book about Paradigm, not in a book about making the system easier to understand.<br /> <br /> You don't add unneeded complexity in the text meant for simplification. It isn't that it put the optional rule, simply, but that it raised the question and choose to answer it in the most complex and unnecessary way instead of explaining the simplest one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464935-health-levels-alternatives?p=1465895#post1465895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, the mandated Spirit is something that the Mage ought to have anyway.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all.<br /> <br /> This was meant for a character that's a shaman Paradigm-wise, not necessarily one that already deals directly with the Umbra, those are two different things.<br /> <br /> I can very well have a Shaman with Life, Time and Correspondence, tapping in the spirits of the world to affect health and see places far in space and time, asking for the spirits of Sympathy to deliver healing effects and so on. I could have Entropy. I could change Matter by asking the spirits of things.<br /> <br /> My Mage could very well be a Shaman that sees the Spirit Sphere as a dangerous and disrespectful imposition over spiritual matters, to be only learned by someone that mastered the humble approach to the spirits (other Spheres) before trying to touch that realm directly instead of asking their intervention.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464935-health-levels-alternatives?p=1465895#post1465895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third, the mandated Spirit doesn't actually impact anything in terms of the practical use of the system\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>It does. The rule mandates Spirit 2, not 1, for every single effect. So you can't ever roll a Level 1 effect. Indeed, you can't even be a shaman with Arete 1.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464935-health-levels-alternatives?p=1465895#post1465895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a bit of a tangent, because I really want to get this off my chest: I've noticed a trend in the X5 game development that we have seen thus far (Vampire, Werewolf, and Hunter); and that is a tendency to borrow heavily from their Chronicles of Darkness counterparts.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Just for the sake of the comment, I think this is heavily overplayed against X5.<br /> <br /> Revised's biggest crime was not really making a proper revision of the systems, despite many glaring issues. X20 couldn't. Now X5 is doing, and in the mean time CoD was the natural place for the actual changes that should have occurred back in Rev.<br /> <br /> So borrowing freely from CoD was just the natural thing to do, but even then they have a lot of other changes that have little to nothing to do with CoD. To me only one or two things seem like unnecessary ports instead of merely inspiration for the changes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464935-health-levels-alternatives?p=1465895#post1465895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">H5 is borrowing so heavily from HtV that is essentially a completely different game than HtR1e\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is still too soon to say if it is really that much Vigil, because the basic concepts are also Hunters Hunted. But it surely isn't HtR for real without the Imbued and that's a huge wtf.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464935-health-levels-alternatives?p=1465895#post1465895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mention this because once they get around to M5, I won't mind if they borrow liberally from MtAw's Arcana.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't even mind the splitting of Entropy, tbh. But indeed, WtAw did it far clearer and better streamlined.<br /> <br /> But I would also like it if they did something that mixed WtAw with the concept of the Pillars, so the system could be better adjusted to each individual Paradigm.<br /> <br /> That would help to reflect better the role of Paradigm on the game. Not an easy thing to do, maybe, but one I would like to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T10:35:40-07:00","id":1465920,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, I'm not complaining about the borrowing; I'm just starting that it's there. As you say, it isn't necessarily a bad thing. <br /> <br /> I have my own thoughts about how to make the Sphere system more adjustable to fit the Focus; in fact, I've put together <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/88705-sphere-variants-for-the-traditions\">four</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385360-fields-for-the-technocracy-reloaded\">separate</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/441968-pillars-for-the-modern-crafts\">rules</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/784502-composite-spheres-for-orphans\">hacks</a> with this in mind. However, that whole approach of variant spheres, pillars, and so on strikes me as messier than it needs to be. I think that for M5, what I'd like to see would be a standardized set of spheres, supplemented by a \u201cMysteries of the Spheres\u201d customized Merit that's gated by Focus and lets you tweak the Spheres to better reflect your views on Magick. For instance, Dimensional Science would become a Mystery of Spirit that gives you more favorable Gauntlet ratings in technological locations; but it can only be taken if your Focus views the Umbra as an alternate dimension, such as what Tychoidean Cosmology describes. Primal Utility would be a Mystery of Prime that requires a Focus that describes Quintessence less as energy and more as value, and allows access to Primal Ventures and easier creation of Wonders. And so on. <br /> <br /> Basically, nine Spheres that are written in a standard, consistent way; and a series of Mysteries that allow you to tweak them in Focus-specific ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T18:37:44-07:00","id":1465965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464935-health-levels-alternatives?p=1465895#post1465895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First, it's entirely optional. Second, the mandated Spirit is something that the Mage ought to have anyway. Third, the mandated Spirit doesn't actually impact anything in terms of the practical use of the system: conjunctional spheres have no effect on the mechanics other than the binary \u201cdo you have what you need to do this?\u201d \u2014 which, going back to the second point, is always \u201cyes\u201d where this option or any variations thereof are concerned. So its biggest crime is that it doesn't do anything useful \u2014 which isn't much of a crime, all things considered, since one of the things it might have done, but didn't, would have been to <i>replace</i> the other Sphere requirements, turning Spirit into an uber-Sphere. So my reaction to it tends to be more along the lines of \u201cmeh\u201d rather than \u201coh, the horror; the horror!\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>I can\u2019t improve on <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> \u2018 response to this but I can add:<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not limited to the optional sidebar. There are other sections that add the sphere tax like psychics needing mind for non-mind phenomena like pyrokinesis. I believe the section for airbender paradigms had similar problems but I need to re-download the book to check.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T11:20:53-07:00","id":1466036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464935-health-levels-alternatives?p=1465965#post1465965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s not limited to the optional sidebar. There are other sections that add the sphere tax like psychics needing mind for non-mind phenomena like pyrokinesis. I believe the section for airbender paradigms had similar problems but I need to re-download the book to check.</div> </div> </div> </div>The section for Airbenders is exactly where it talks about the Spirit Sphere. It is actually weirder than that as it talks about a convoluted topic without enough context or reaching any conclusion before presenting the optional rule.<br /> <br /> And yes, it is all over the place. The author can't differentiate between the two elements of the Game, Sphere and Paradigm, and so it puts a lot of stress on how you describe the effect instead of what is the effect itself. It is basically using unrelated Spheres as Instruments.<br /> <br /> Considering the book's intent it isn't bad. It is horrible. It is bad for people that have enough of a grasp of the system to correct the book. But those are not the target of the book. To inform people that still have actual difficulty grasping the system it is a profound disservice and makes the game even more complex and taxing than it needs to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T10:42:38-07:00","id":1466149,"title":"","content":"I pulled up HDYDT again. I remember why I deleted it the first time. My brain hurts.<br /> <br /> The needless sphere taxes are all over the book. Often the book contradicts itself within one or two pages of saying something. The Airbender section is ill thought out both in what it says and what it doesn't. The Levitation and flight sections are so very much worse. Within two paragraphs the book manages manages to:<br /> <br /> - introduce a paradigm based sphere tax<br /> - introduce a non-paradigm based sphere tax,<br /> - demonstrate a complete and total misunderstanding of what locking an effect is and how you do it.<br /> - demonstrate a complete and total misunderstanding of the difference between affecting something and altering something<br /> <br /> AND<br /> <br /> - show an example that contradicts all of the above<br /> <br /> Anyways, this is threatening to turn this thread into a HDYDT complaint fest so I'll stop.<br /> <br /> <br /> Suffice to say, my advice is:<br /> <br /> Require the smallest combination of spheres available that will produce the desired effect. Never add extra sphere requirements for paradigm for the exact same effect, and never add extra sphere requirements for balance reasons unless there is no other way. If the sphere isn't doing something tangible, it shouldn't be there. Expect consistency between similar things (e.g. If you don't need to add Matter to cast a spell on an object you don't need Life to cast an equivalent effect on something living). Any exceptions to these should have well stated reasons and explanations. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T12:29:39-07:00","id":1466152,"title":"","content":"I want to hit double-like on Ramnesis' post there. mage is complicated enough compared to many RPGs out there. Don't make it *more* complicated than it needs to be, except in cases where it's a creative idea by a player that just hits the Rule Of Cool and causes fun for your players instead of frustration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T13:36:23-07:00","id":1466161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464935-health-levels-alternatives?p=1466036#post1466036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, it is all over the place. The author can't differentiate between the two elements of the Game, Sphere and Paradigm, and so it puts a lot of stress on how you describe the effect instead of what is the effect itself. It is basically using unrelated Spheres as Instruments.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never read HDYDT through cover-to-cover, and I'm not experienced enough with the Mage system to recognize all of the flaws. But I think this particular point hits on how I've always interpreted this optional(?) rule. I've tended to consider it more from the perspective of Psionics, which is a downright busted Practice/Instrument compared to what a lot of other Mages have to work with if you are letting them just produce an Effect by thinking about it. For pure Psionics, just think-it-and-it-happens, I don't necessarily consider it unreasonable to add a Sphere tax for what would otherwise a cheap way of being able to cast without an Instrument without admitting that's what you're doing. If you want to add on some kind of Instrument, like meditation, different story.<br /> <br /> Similarly, you might imagine that a Shaman might want (or need) to skip a sacred dance or chiminage ritual and just get something done by going straight to the spirits in question. If they don't want to treat that as casting without an Instrument, giving them the option of throwing the Spirit Sphere on in order to give them a &quot;direct connection&quot; with the spirits might be a way to interpret it.<br /> <br /> In either case, it only makes sense if 1) the Sphere is being used as an Instrument, and 2) if that Sphere or its related concepts have a central enough place in their Paradigm/Focus that it could be used in that fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T14:25:18-07:00","id":1466170,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't bother with a Sphere tax; as I said in my last post, those don't do anything if you already have the Sphere in question. <br /> <br /> I do agree that Psionics is a broken Practice if you approach it as \u201cconcentrate and things happen\u201d. That's not a Practice; that's Working Without Focus, and costs a point of Willpower and +3 difficulty. Bear with me a moment:<br /> <br /> I've mentioned before that I like to generalize the \u201cTakes Extra Time\u201d Magickal Modifier to serve as a \u201cuses onerous instrument\u201d modifier: it may be onerous because it takes longer to use, or because it's not particularly mobile (cauldrons vs. broomsticks, for example), or for other reasons. But whatever the reason happens to be, if the instrument that you're using is particularly inconvenient to use, it's worth -1 to -3 difficulty on the Arete roll. The motivation for this is primarily a gamist one: why would a player use an onerous Instrument if there's no benefit for doing so? And the answer is that there <i>is</i> a benefit to doing so, though it's an indirect one: some Instruments are more effective than others, which is represented by them granting a negative Magickal Modifier; but these more effective Instruments also tend to come with drawbacks. Thus, they're \u201cmore onerous\u201d to use them typical Instruments. If this wasn't so, then these more effective Instruments would be used by everyone, for everything. Mages aren't idiots. <br /> <br /> But conversely, I tend to adapt the \u201cWorking Without Focus\u201d mechanic to the opposite effect: if the instrument that you're using is exceptionally <i>convenient</i>, to the point that it's almost as if you're not using an Instrument at all, then by a similar line of reasoning, they should come with a \u201cdifficulty tax\u201d of up to +3 difficulty; and for the most extreme ones, possibly even a \u201cWillpower tax\u201d. <br /> <br /> So you want your psychic to just go around wielding Forces through simple concentration? That's +3 Difficulty and 1 WP, just like if you're trying to Work Without Focus \u2014 because you basically are. Or, you could put in the work to devise a set of Instruments for your Psionics that <i>aren't</i> \u201cjust concentrate, and it happens\u201d \u2014 say, a reliance on crystals or dowsing rods \u2014 and you get to bypass those prices, or at least mitigate them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-01-2021, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T14:36:21-07:00","id":1466172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464935-health-levels-alternatives?p=1466161#post1466161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In either case, it only makes sense if 1) the Sphere is being used as an Instrument, and 2) if that Sphere or its related concepts have a central enough place in their Paradigm/Focus that it could be used in that fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is that Sphere isn't Instrument, even if they seem to be central to a given Paradigm. After all, if this is the case, then you're still letting those Paradigms cast without Instrument just because they have the most magical Sphere according to themselves.<br /> <br /> A psychic still must define their paradigm enough for the ST to grasp what is the difference between with and without Instrument. The best way to handle it is to ask two simple questions:<br /> <br /> 1- Can you picture a situation where this character can't cast, while most Mages would be able to?<br /> <br /> 2- Can you picture <b>any</b> non-magical trait playing a role in letting the character do stuff?<br /> <br /> One of the simplest answers for a psychic is that doing stuff just with the mind requires a lot of concentration, so doing it without proper focus setup requires a roll, maybe Willpower, maybe Wits + something or Perception + something. As ST you decide if the character benefits from the roll to reduce dif, but at least one success is needed simply to be able to roll Arete.<br /> <br /> Done, you have a proper Instrument. It isn't visible, but put limits and context all the same.<br /> <br /> Later, with time, you'll getting to the more complex question of how the Paradigm affects the possibility of an effect, but that's far more complex anyway.<br /> <br /> Without that you didn't really solved anything. Mind and Spirit are like every other Spheres and need an Instrument, that's one of the reasons they shouldn't be used as Instruments. A psychic isn't excused to ignore Instrument because they have Mind and a shaman isn't excused to ignore Instrument because they have Spirit.<br /> <br /> By making this kind of rule, you're only making the game harder for everyone and keeping the players from making creative effects instead of really keeping them from being broken if that's a concern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T15:46:48-07:00","id":1466185,"title":"","content":"A Sphere tax doesn't hurt you if you have the Sphere in question, but it means that you need up to double the total number of dots in Spheres for any Effect that falls outside the Instrument-Sphere itself, which isn't nothing. Your way of handling it sounds pretty reasonable, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a>, though I would say that I tend to view &quot;Psionics&quot; as distinct from &quot;New Age&quot; stuff like crystals and reiki. But that's more pop-cultural influence than anything else.<br /> <br /> I should note that I've had this idea bouncing around in my head for days while reading this thread, and I was kind of aware that it was just a random thought/charitable interpretation. I only decided to voice it when <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> literally used the expression &quot;Spheres as Instruments,&quot; and I was like 'yes, that's what I've been thinking.' I also want to hit on the term &quot;unrelated Spheres,&quot; because while the Spheres may be unrelated to the Effect, they are not unrelated to the Paradigm. Which yes, is probably not how Spheres were intended to be used, but I think the idea itself is interesting at least. And I only think it could ever be appropriate when the concepts of one particular Sphere play a truly foundational role in the cosmology or metaphysics of the Mage in question. It shouldn't be a cheat that any Mage can @$$pull with some fast-talking. I'm not so much advocating for the idea as musing about it, though.<br /> <br /> Regarding when said Instruments would be uniquely disadvantaged, I must definitely admit that the Psychic is severely advantaged, as theoretically they would be capable of magic as long as they were capable of thought. Whereas I feel you would literally need to invent some kind of anti-psi MacGuffin to deal with the Psychic, I could imagine some situations where the spiritual landscape is so suppressed or damaged that direct action through the Spirit Sphere could be impaired or impossible, but it's still an extreme scenario.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T15:51:31-07:00","id":1466187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464935-health-levels-alternatives?p=1466152#post1466152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to hit double-like on Ramnesis' post there. mage is complicated enough compared to many RPGs out there. Don't make it *more* complicated than it needs to be, except in cases where it's a creative idea by a player that just hits the Rule Of Cool and causes fun for your players instead of frustration.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm of two minds on this: on the one hand, I sometimes wonder if Mage wouldn't be better off using a fundamentally different game engine that's even more lightweight and freeform than the Storyteller System: something like Chad Underkoffler's Prose Descriptive Qualities (PDQ) system (e.g., Truth &amp; Justice) or Fred Hicks' Fate system. Basically, take the open nature of the Spheres and apply it to <i>everything</i>. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, I'm not sure that the problem with Mage is that it's overly complicated so much as it's under-defined. There's a <i>lot</i> of stuff, especially in the Magick system, that relies on the Storyteller making everything up on his own, as opposed to making that an option. It could also do with better organization; but let me focus on the \u201cmore definition\u201d for now. <br /> <br /> I mentioned earlier that I wouldn't mind if the hypothetical M5 borrows heavily from <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>. Mostly, I was thinking of this in terms of MtAw1e, which, as monteparnas pointed out, was basically the MRev team implementing lessons learned from MRev. But I also wouldn't mind if M20 were to implement something like MtAw2e's Yantras in the form of a more defined Focus system for M20. The trick would be doing it in a way that enhances the game rather than overcomplicating it. Something along the lines of Effects requiring a certain amount of Instrumental support and benefitting from extra support, while something like the Yantras system is used to rate how much support a given Instrument gives. <br /> <br /> And on another note, but related to the idea of more definition, I sometimes wonder if M5 should bring Steve Kenson (<b>Trinity Continuum: Aberrant</b>) on board to build an Effects-based foundation for Magick, similar to what he did for Aberrant but more open-ended: that is, let him handle the crunchy side of things (what are the game systems for the various Effects that are possible?), while working within the framework of \u201cwhich Effects you can use is determined primarily by what Spheres you have, and what you can do with them is determined by how many successes you achieve\u201d. I'm actually thinking of this in terms of the work he put into <b>Mutants &amp; Masterminds</b>, where he managed to capture the sheer diversity of powers that show up in superhero settings in 66 pages, as opposed to the 136 pages in <b>How Do You Do That?</b> which attempts a similar feat with notably less success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-01-2021, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T16:37:10-07:00","id":1466201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464935-health-levels-alternatives?p=1466185#post1466185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding when said Instruments would be uniquely disadvantaged, I must definitely admit that the Psychic is severely advantaged, as theoretically they would be capable of magic as long as they were capable of thought. Whereas I feel you would literally need to invent some kind of anti-psi MacGuffin to deal with the Psychic, I could imagine some situations where the spiritual landscape is so suppressed or damaged that direct action through the Spirit Sphere could be impaired or impossible, but it's still an extreme scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>The psychic is only severely advantage if you assume that they can act freely as long as they can think. Which is a fair assumption, but not the only valid one. I would then go by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a>'s approach of just asking for the same cost as Working Without Focus.<br /> <br /> Neither approach is wrong between those two. What constitutes Instrument for your Paradigm is something the player should define anyway, so no particular view of what a psychic is wins the day.<br /> <br /> More specifically, from a design standpoint, the problem with accepting the use of a Sphere as Instrument is that it puts a clear advantage on that one combination of Paradigm + Sphere. If psychics can Work Without Focus and not pay the price if they have Mind (a particularly useful Sphere to begin with), then you have an in-built encouragement for players building Mind-using Psychics.<br /> <br /> Instead of encouraging exploration, you encourage conformity, and each pairing of Paradigm + Sphere becomes an &quot;optimized choice&quot;. Which isn't a bad thing <i>per se</i> depending on setting and narrative goals, but seems contrary to the themes of Mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464935-health-levels-alternatives?p=1466187#post1466187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, I'm not sure that the problem with Mage is that it's overly complicated so much as it's under-defined.</div> </div> </div> </div>The part about the system I think it unfortunately can't be expected. We can homerule it, but Mage will stay using the same system as the rest of the WoD.<br /> <br /> But this part is surely true. When I say <i>complicated</i>, at least, it is less that the system is complex and more that it is hard to wrap your head around and left too much for you to decide. It is beautiful on paper, but not so much on play, unless you already have a very clear mental picture of what you want to do with it anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464935-health-levels-alternatives?p=1466187#post1466187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mentioned earlier that I wouldn't mind if the hypothetical M5 borrows heavily from <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>MtAw2e is the system evolving from 1e as 1e evolved from Rev. The big problem of the cWoD era was not applying what they learned with WoD directly in WoD.<br /> <br /> But yes, the Yantra system wraps up a lot of things about Instruments very nicely, and isn't really less versatile in describing a Paradigm even if it isn't a thing in Awakening. Their Paradox system is also a lot better, although it would certainly need some tweaking.<br /> <br /> The point being, all those rules are better in Awakening because they're better defined. You're not left in the air until a stroke of genius hits you and you understands the magic system. Instead it is very friendly for you to use before you start to get into its deeps.<br /> <br /> Ascension only work at all when you start to wrap your mind around its deeps.<br /> <br /> I also think their take on Rotes is better and should be imported. Rotes help a lot to define Paradigm and guide some themes in Mage, like how any grimoire is theoretically a treasure, but actually doesn't matter since the Rotes within don't matter. And more importantly, Rotes are a <b>huge</b> help to new players and Storytellers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464935-health-levels-alternatives?p=1466187#post1466187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And on another note, but related to the idea of more definition, I sometimes wonder if M5 should bring Steve Kenson (<b>Trinity Continuum: Aberrant</b>)</div> </div> </div> </div>I never read <b>Aberrant </b>to know, but as I read the paragraph I was thinking about how nice it would be to have something like <b>M&amp;M 2ed <i>Ultimate Power</i></b>. That's a wonderful take on essentially the same problem, and yet instead of making the game harder, it made it easier. And instead of taxing the player, it gave them even more tools to run their imaginations wild while building their own power systems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T05:50:18-07:00","id":1466270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1464935-health-levels-alternatives?p=1466187#post1466187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm of two minds on this: on the one hand, I sometimes wonder if Mage wouldn't be better off using a fundamentally different game engine that's even more lightweight and freeform than the Storyteller System: something like Chad Underkoffler's Prose Descriptive Qualities (PDQ) system (e.g., Truth &amp; Justice) or Fred Hicks' Fate system. Basically, take the open nature of the Spheres and apply it to <i>everything</i>.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I'm not sure that the problem with Mage is that it's overly complicated so much as it's under-defined. There's a <i>lot</i> of stuff, especially in the Magick system, that relies on the Storyteller making everything up on his own, as opposed to making that an option. It could also do with better organization; but let me focus on the \u201cmore definition\u201d for now.</div> </div> </div> </div>It definitely appears underdefined in some areas, in the sense that there are implicit assumptions that are used freely without ever saying why. There seems to be an unstated rule that Life is inherently harder to target than Matter, for instance, to the point that targeting people requires adding Life while targeting objects does not require adding Matter. However, I don't think that's an indication that the magic system needs more definition. I largely think the hidden assumptions are in the way and most of the 'problems' they address are better handled with other aspects of the system like success requirements, skill checks, and difficulty modifiers.<br /> <br /> I have considered porting some WoD games over to Fate in the past, but I haven't considered it for Mage. Fate works best when you can make the system say something about the nature of the world, so I'd need to see what tweaks promote a world of Reality on the Brink.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}